# Sample forbidden URLs file for go-polipo.  -*-sh-*-
# Point the forbiddenFile (or uncachableFile) configuration variable at this.
#
# forbiddenTunnelsFile uses the same file format, but matches CONNECT
# (HTTPS tunnel) targets differently: a domain line must match the host
# exactly (no subdomains), and a regex is matched against the raw
# "host:port" from the CONNECT request rather than a "http://" URL.

# Forbid all hosts belonging to a given domain name:

#counter.com
#hitbox.com
#doubleclick.net
#www.cashcount.com

# Forbid all hosts contaning a string matching a given regex.  Note
# that you need to quote dots, so that a regex is not misinterpreted
# as a domain name.

#^http://[^/]*counter\.com
#/ads/
#/phpAdsNew
#counting\.php
